-- | A reference distributor for signature-based delivery. Such a distributor's
-- entire on-ledger obligation is one contract: hold the public key on a template
-- the distributor signs, implement `DistributorKey` so consumers can read it,
-- and disclose it to them.
--
-- Everything else happens off-ledger or on the consumer's side. The distributor
-- signs payloads with the matching private key outside Daml and delivers them by
-- whatever channel it likes; the consumer verifies them inside its own choice
-- using `canton-data-standard-codecs`. There is no verifier interface and no
-- verify choice here. A distributor publishes a key; it does not run
-- verifications on behalf of consumers.
--
-- The publication is long-lived and contention-free: a read never archives it,
-- and one contract authenticates every feed and every payload the key signs, so
-- no number of consumers verifying concurrently can conflict.
module DistributorKeyProducer.Publication where

import DataStandard.DistributorKeyV1

-- | A distributor's published signing key. Created once and disclosed to
-- consumers, who read it through the `DistributorKey` interface and never import
-- this module.
--
-- The scheme fields (`signMethod`, `hashMethod`) are fixed by the standard and set
-- to their constants in the view. `payloadCodec` is a template field, because
-- which envelope a key signs is the distributor's configuration: one key signs
-- quotes, another signs data points, and a product may advertise a codec of its
-- own.
template DistributorKeyPublication
  with
    distributor : Party
      -- ^ The distributor; signs and owns the publication, and is the party whose
      -- signatures this key validates.
    publicKey : Text
      -- ^ The distributor's hex DER-SPKI secp256k1 public key.
    payloadCodec : Text
      -- ^ The envelope this key signs, for example the codecs package's
      -- `quoteHashCodecId`. A consumer's verification refuses a key whose codec is
      -- not the one it verifies against, so this field is what binds a key to a
      -- payload shape.
  where
    signatory distributor

    interface instance DistributorKey for DistributorKeyPublication where
      view = DistributorKeyView with
        distributor
        publicKey
        signMethod = "secp256k1"
        hashMethod = "SHA-256"
        payloadCodec

    -- | Rotate the signing key by archiving this publication and creating its
    -- replacement carrying the new key.
    --
    -- Payloads signed under the old key stop verifying the moment this contract is
    -- archived, because a consumer can no longer read the old key: the archived
    -- contract id resolves for nobody, disclosed or not. Payloads signed under the
    -- new key verify against the replacement, which the distributor discloses in
    -- turn. How a consumer learns that rotation happened sits outside the
    -- standard, in the distribution relationship.
    choice RotateKey : ContractId DistributorKeyPublication
      with
        newPublicKey : Text
          -- ^ The distributor's new hex DER-SPKI secp256k1 public key.
      controller distributor
      do create this with publicKey = newPublicKey
